    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"A four-layer digital model of the groundwater system of the Cretaceous-age Coastal Plain aquifers of South Carolina was developed using the MODFLOW program by McDonald and Harbaugh (1988). Results of the study are described in a report by Campbell and van Heeswijk (in press). Although that report summarizes the data input to the model, detailed documentation of model input and model output has not been published. This report, which is a supplement to the report by Campbell and van Heeswijk (in press), provides detailed, electronic documentation of the model data.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
